	spec: 'Web tool cards follow the visible-plumbing rule (AGENTS.md). A closed card shows one line: the description, and the session-local call number on the right. An open Bash card reads like the terminal: `$ command` (`& command` when backgrounded), multiline commands preserved; declared modifies as one line, "Edits a.ts, src/commands/*.ts"; a non-default timeout only if set; then output streaming as it arrives, a glimpse of long output, as in the terminal, with a control that shows all of it, and the exit status when nonzero. Other tools head the card with their description, else their name and first text argument (notify: its text); an open head wraps, so a one-line headline argument is not repeated below, and other arguments show once as "key: value". Results show without labels. Cards never show call IDs, argument types, "omitted arguments and defaults" or execution-control sections; invalid or unfamiliar arguments and rejection reasons do show. src/common/tool-details.ts shrinks or goes to match; the terminal renderer is the reference and should share code where it reduces lines.',
